('127.603.d.5.E',3,'Photos, completed checklists, and supervisor notes are examples of representative work:','["gifts", "rumors", "samples", "debts"]'::jsonb,2,'Samples show real skills in action.','original'),
('127.603.d.5.E',4,'Collecting work samples during a practicum helps a student build a:','["lease", "budget", "contract", "portfolio"]'::jsonb,3,'Samples are used to show employers what you can do.','original'),
('127.604.d.1.A',3,'An event planner who joins a professional association and takes industry workshops is working toward career advancement and lifelong:','["learning", "rivalry", "spending", "silence"]'::jsonb,0,'Ongoing learning keeps skills current.','original'),
('127.604.d.1.A',4,'Earning a certified meeting professional credential is a strategy to enhance a planner''s:','["office size", "career prospects", "parking space", "vacation days"]'::jsonb,1,'Credentials signal expertise to employers.','original'),
('127.604.d.1.B',3,'A global health emergency that cancels large gatherings shows how historical events can reshape the:','["weather forecast", "school calendar", "event industry", "tax code"]'::jsonb,2,'Major events change how planners work.','original'),
('127.604.d.1.B',4,'After a major disruption, planners often add virtual and hybrid options, which shows how history drives:','["staff vacations", "menu repeats", "price freezes", "industry change"]'::jsonb,3,'Planners adapt to new realities.','original'),
('127.604.d.1.C',3,'A planner prepares a backup indoor space in case a storm threatens an outdoor wedding. This is a plan that addresses current:','["conditions", "uniforms", "menus", "trophies"]'::jsonb,0,'Plans respond to what is happening now.','original'),
('127.604.d.1.C',4,'When travel prices rise sharply, a planner might respond by choosing a closer venue or offering a:','["dress code", "virtual option", "longer agenda", "bigger budget"]'::jsonb,1,'Good plans adapt to current events.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
insert into public.question_bank (teks_code, teks_item_id, subject, grade_num, course, difficulty, qtype, prompt, choices, answer_idx, explanation, source, status, gen_batch)
select distinct on (v.prompt) v.code, i.id, d.subject,
       case when i.grade_level = 'K' then 0 when i.grade_level ~ '^[0-9]+' then substring(i.grade_level from '^[0-9]+')::smallint end,
       case when i.grade_level is null then i.grade_course_title end,
       v.diff, 'mc', v.prompt, v.choices, v.ans, v.expl, v.src, 'checked', 'cte_78_v1'
from (values
('127.604.d.1.D',3,'A planner keeps vendor contracts as scanned files and a printed binder. This documents knowledge in electronic and:','["random formats", "verbal formats only", "manual formats", "secret formats"]'::jsonb,2,'Records can be stored on paper and on a computer.','original'),
('127.604.d.1.D',4,'Keeping a digital checklist of past events helps a planner reuse what worked, which is a form of documenting:','["rumors", "menu fonts", "guest gossip", "technical knowledge"]'::jsonb,3,'Written records preserve know-how.','original'),
('127.604.d.1.E',3,'A student prepares a collection of resumes, event plans, and photos from past events to present to employers. This is a professional:','["portfolio", "budget", "contract", "invoice"]'::jsonb,0,'Portfolios showcase experience.','original'),
('127.604.d.1.E',4,'When presenting a portfolio, the best order is usually to start with your strongest items and explain your:','["weekend plans", "role in each project", "salary demands", "favorite foods"]'::jsonb,1,'Employers want to know what you contributed.','original'),
('127.604.d.1.F',3,'A candidate compares two planner jobs: one pays more, and the other includes health coverage and training. The candidate is comparing salaries and:','["rumors", "venues", "benefits", "menus"]'::jsonb,2,'Total pay includes benefits.','original'),
('127.604.d.1.F',4,'A job paying $48,000 with no benefits versus $46,000 plus paid insurance might be worth the same or more because benefits add:','["risk", "debt", "tax", "value"]'::jsonb,3,'Insurance and time off carry real worth.','original'),
('127.604.d.1.G',3,'A planner tracks monthly pay, rent, and food to see how much can go to savings. This is a personal:','["budget", "floor plan", "agenda", "guest list"]'::jsonb,0,'Budgets plan income and spending.','original'),
('127.604.d.1.G',4,'A planner paid irregularly by event should set aside money in busy months to cover slower ones, which is part of personal:','["sponsor relations", "money management", "event marketing", "venue scouting"]'::jsonb,1,'Irregular income needs careful planning.','original'),
('127.604.d.2.A',3,'Introducing guests properly, using titles, and saying ''thank you'' to vendors are examples of professional:','["catering", "décor", "etiquette", "accounting"]'::jsonb,2,'Etiquette shows respect.','original'),
('127.604.d.2.A',4,'At a formal dinner, the host usually stands to greet arriving guests, showing proper social:','["budgeting", "pricing", "math", "manners"]'::jsonb,3,'Correct manners help guests feel welcome.','original'),
('127.604.d.2.B',3,'Using a clear subject line and a polite greeting in an email to a client is correct electronic communication:','["etiquette", "price", "menu", "tax"]'::jsonb,0,'Online messages should be courteous.','original'),
('127.604.d.2.B',4,'Typing in all capital letters in a business email can seem like:','["humor", "shouting", "politeness", "whispering"]'::jsonb,1,'All caps comes across as rude.','original'),
('127.604.d.2.C',3,'A hospitality code of ethics asks professionals to treat everyone fairly and protect:','["their own profits only", "gossip", "client information", "their competitors"]'::jsonb,2,'Codes guide honest conduct.','original'),
('127.604.d.2.C',4,'A code of ethics for the profession is meant to guide planners in situations where the right action is:','["always clear", "irrelevant", "illegal", "not obvious"]'::jsonb,3,'Codes help with difficult choices.','original'),
('127.604.d.2.D',3,'A vendor offers a planner a private gift in exchange for choosing their services over cheaper ones. The most ethical course is to:','["decline and disclose it", "accept quietly", "raise the price", "hide it from the client"]'::jsonb,0,'Conflicts of interest should be avoided or revealed.','original'),
('127.604.d.2.D',4,'When two choices both seem acceptable, the most ethical choice is the one that is honest, fair, and:','["hides risks", "protects the client", "saves the planner time", "earns a bonus"]'::jsonb,1,'Ethics puts others'' interests alongside your own.','original'),
('127.604.d.3.A',3,'A planner who finishes tasks early, keeps files neat, and does not quit when a problem arises shows organization and:','["rivalry", "avoidance", "perseverance", "gossip"]'::jsonb,2,'Perseverance means sticking with the task.','original'),
('127.604.d.3.A',4,'Essential workplace traits for planners include dependability, flexibility, and:','["idleness", "arrogance", "secrecy", "attention to detail"]'::jsonb,3,'Small details make events succeed.','original'),
('127.604.d.3.B',3,'Assigning roles, sharing credit, and communicating openly help a planning team build:','["trust", "blame", "conflict", "delay"]'::jsonb,0,'Strong teams depend on trust.','original'),
('127.604.d.3.B',4,'A good team leader at an event briefing makes sure every member knows their:','["hobbies", "role", "salary", "age"]'::jsonb,1,'Clear roles prevent confusion.','original'),
('127.604.d.3.C',3,'By asking questions about a client''s goals, guest count, and budget, a planner learns the client''s:','["age", "hobbies", "needs", "height"]'::jsonb,2,'Questions uncover expectations.','original'),
('127.604.d.3.C',4,'A client says the event ''should feel elegant but not stuffy.'' A planner responds well by asking for examples and:','["changing topics", "ignoring the comment", "assuming", "clarifying details"]'::jsonb,3,'Clarifying avoids misunderstandings.','original'),
('127.604.d.3.D',3,'Leadership on event day includes anticipating problems, such as a late caterer, and:','["defusing them calmly", "ignoring them", "blaming staff", "panicking"]'::jsonb,0,'Leaders stay calm and act.','original'),
('127.604.d.3.D',4,'A leader who notices a long registration line opens a second check-in table. This shows leadership by:','["cutting the budget", "anticipating an issue", "ignoring guests", "delegating blame"]'::jsonb,1,'Fixing a problem early prevents bigger ones.','original'),
('127.604.d.3.E',3,'A client wants live music, but the venue bans amplified sound. A planner can negotiate a compromise such as:','["a larger venue fee", "ignoring the rule", "acoustic performers", "no entertainment"]'::jsonb,2,'Negotiation seeks a solution both sides accept.','original'),
('127.604.d.3.E',4,'Which approach best resolves a conflict between a client and a vendor?','["blame the vendor", "pick the cheaper side", "avoid both parties", "listen to both sides and find common ground"]'::jsonb,3,'Win-win outcomes preserve relationships.','original'),
('127.604.d.4.A',3,'Terms like ''banquet event order,'' ''load-in,'' and ''attrition'' are examples of event industry:','["vocabulary", "recipes", "fabrics", "maps"]'::jsonb,0,'Professionals share a common language.','original'),
('127.604.d.4.A',4,'The time vendors arrive to set up equipment before an event is called:','["service", "load-in", "breakdown", "strike"]'::jsonb,1,'Load-in is the setup arrival time.','original'),
('127.604.d.4.B',3,'A planner sends each vendor a written timeline so everyone arrives on time. This is a procedure to ensure client needs are:','["unknown", "argued", "met", "delayed"]'::jsonb,2,'Procedures make sure details are handled.','original'),
('127.604.d.4.B',4,'A site visit before booking a venue helps a planner confirm that the space fits the client''s needs, capacity, and:','["size of the logo", "favorite colors", "vendor''s age", "accessibility"]'::jsonb,3,'Visits reveal practical issues.','original'),
('127.604.d.4.C',3,'A company that controls costs, keeps a steady client base, and prices fairly is structured for:','["profitability", "closure", "failure", "loss"]'::jsonb,0,'Good structure supports profit.','original'),
('127.604.d.4.C',4,'A very small event company may keep costs low by outsourcing specialists as needed instead of hiring many:','["planners", "full-time staff", "clients", "vendors"]'::jsonb,1,'Flexible staffing reduces fixed costs.','original'),
('127.604.d.4.D',3,'Before an event, the planner and client sign a written agreement that spells out services, fees, and cancellation terms. This is a:','["menu", "invoice", "contract", "receipt"]'::jsonb,2,'Contracts protect both parties.','original'),
('127.604.d.4.D',4,'During an event, the planner follows the run-of-show, a minute-by-minute:','["recipe", "guest list", "budget", "schedule"]'::jsonb,3,'The run-of-show keeps the event on time.','original'),
('127.604.d.4.E',3,'Checking supply lists, confirming staff schedules, and reviewing the day''s events are tasks for a planner''s daily:','["operations", "vacation", "marketing", "hiring"]'::jsonb,0,'Organization keeps the office running.','original'),
('127.604.d.4.E',4,'The best way to organize daily work is to list tasks and rank them by:','["length of name", "urgency and importance", "alphabetical order", "color"]'::jsonb,1,'Prioritizing keeps deadlines.','original'),
('127.604.d.4.F',3,'The growth of online ticket sales and social media changed how events are advertised. This is a societal shift that shaped the:','["weather", "climate", "industry", "calendar"]'::jsonb,2,'Society''s changes affect the business.','original'),
('127.604.d.4.F',4,'Increased interest in sustainability led many planners to reduce waste at events. This is an example of a:','["new holiday", "tax cut", "price freeze", "societal trend"]'::jsonb,3,'Public values shape practices.','original'),
('127.604.d.4.G',3,'A city organization that promotes tourism and helps groups find venues is a convention and visitors'':','["bureau", "court", "bank", "school"]'::jsonb,0,'These bureaus help bring events to a city.','original'),
('127.604.d.4.G',4,'A convention and visitors'' bureau can give planners destination information, hotel contacts, and:','["passports", "local referrals", "loans", "tax returns"]'::jsonb,1,'Bureaus connect planners with local resources.','original'),
('127.604.d.5.A',3,'Guests may have different dietary, language, and accessibility needs. These are the varying needs of:','["banks", "suppliers", "customers", "inspectors"]'::jsonb,2,'Planners serve diverse guests.','original'),
('127.604.d.5.A',4,'A client with guests using wheelchairs needs a venue with ramps and:','["narrow doors", "steep stairs", "low lighting", "accessible restrooms"]'::jsonb,3,'Accessibility is essential planning.','original'),
('127.604.d.5.B',3,'Respecting individual differences means treating each guest with:','["courtesy and fairness", "impatience", "indifference", "bias"]'::jsonb,0,'Respect applies to everyone.','original'),
('127.604.d.5.B',4,'A planner who learns that a guest cannot eat certain foods for religious reasons arranges a suitable menu. This shows respect for individual:','["savings", "differences", "dates", "tickets"]'::jsonb,1,'Honoring needs shows respect.','original'),
('127.604.d.5.C',3,'Meeting varying needs is important because it makes all attendees feel:','["confused", "ignored", "welcome", "excluded"]'::jsonb,2,'Inclusion improves the guest experience.','original'),
('127.604.d.5.C',4,'If a planner ignores special requests, the likely result is unhappy guests and a damaged:','["budget line", "floor plan", "calendar", "reputation"]'::jsonb,3,'Service quality builds a planner''s name.','original'),
('127.604.d.5.D',3,'A business plan for an event company serving both corporate and wedding clients must address the needs of:','["each market", "no market", "competitors only", "only one market"]'::jsonb,0,'Plans should match audience needs.','original'),
('127.604.d.5.D',4,'A company that wants to attract clients from many cultures should plan for multilingual materials and flexible:','["logos", "services", "parking", "pricing only"]'::jsonb,1,'Business plans must be adaptable.','original'),
('127.604.d.5.E',3,'Greetings, gift giving, and dress expectations differ between cultures. These are differences in social:','["wiring", "taxes", "etiquette", "inventory"]'::jsonb,2,'Knowing customs prevents mistakes.','original'),
('127.604.d.5.E',4,'When planning an international business meeting, a planner should research local business customs, including:','["weather only", "sports scores", "stock prices", "greetings and dress"]'::jsonb,3,'Cultural research prevents offense.','original'),
('127.604.d.6.A',3,'Virtual reality venue tours and event apps are examples of emerging technologies that planners can use to:','["improve the guest experience", "raise taxes", "reduce guest count", "cancel events"]'::jsonb,0,'New tools help planners serve clients.','original'),
('127.604.d.6.A',4,'Before adopting a new technology, a planner should consider its cost, ease of use, and benefit to:','["inspectors", "clients", "landlords", "competitors"]'::jsonb,1,'Technology must serve a purpose.','original'),
('127.604.d.6.B',3,'A computer program that tracks registrations, budgets, and vendor contacts in one place is event planning:','["stationery", "furniture", "software", "décor"]'::jsonb,2,'It helps organize the work.','original'),
('127.604.d.6.B',4,'An advantage of using planning software over paper lists is that updates can be shared with the team:','["only monthly", "by mail", "never", "instantly"]'::jsonb,3,'Digital tools keep everyone current.','original'),
('127.604.d.6.C',3,'A slide show with video clips, music, and animation is a complex:','["multimedia presentation", "phone call", "written memo", "table plan"]'::jsonb,0,'Multimedia combines several media types.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
