('127.604.d.6.C',4,'When presenting to a client, crowded slides with too much text are less effective than clear visuals and:','["long paragraphs", "brief key points", "tiny fonts", "dense tables"]'::jsonb,1,'Simple slides communicate better.','original'),
('127.604.d.6.D',3,'At a trade show booth, the device that records sales and processes card payments is a point-of-sale:','["badge", "menu", "system", "license"]'::jsonb,2,'POS systems handle transactions.','original'),
('127.604.d.6.D',4,'An event organizer who uses a point-of-sale system can quickly see:','["vendor birthdays", "weather forecasts", "guest ages", "what sold"]'::jsonb,3,'POS data supports reports and decisions.','original'),
('127.604.d.6.E',3,'A planner decides to use the company website, email lists, and social media to sell tickets. These are Internet resources used to maximize:','["profitability", "costs", "errors", "delays"]'::jsonb,0,'Online tools reach more buyers.','original'),
('127.604.d.6.E',4,'A plan for using Internet resources should include goals, a schedule, and a way to measure:','["rumors", "results", "moods", "hobbies"]'::jsonb,1,'Measurement shows what works.','original'),
('127.604.d.6.F',3,'Sending quick updates to vendors through a group messaging tool is an electronic communication tool for:','["decoration", "dancing", "planning", "subtraction"]'::jsonb,2,'Digital tools speed communication.','original'),
('127.604.d.6.F',4,'An online registration form that collects payments is an electronic tool used for:','["parking only", "cooking only", "cleaning only", "selling and planning"]'::jsonb,3,'Forms handle sales and details.','original'),
('127.604.d.7.A',3,'A company that provides funding for an event in exchange for advertising is the event''s:','["sponsor", "caterer", "vendor", "guest"]'::jsonb,0,'Sponsors provide financial support.','original'),
('127.604.d.7.A',4,'The person who coordinates the planning and day-to-day running of an event is the:','["guest speaker", "organizer", "sponsor", "attendee"]'::jsonb,1,'Organizers manage logistics.','original'),
('127.604.d.7.B',3,'A planner compares prices, quality, and reliability of rental companies before choosing a:','["guest", "banner", "supplier", "sponsor"]'::jsonb,2,'Selecting suppliers affects cost and quality.','original'),
('127.604.d.7.B',4,'Before signing with a supplier, the planner should check references and read the:','["guest list", "menu twice", "time zone", "contract carefully"]'::jsonb,3,'Contracts spell out obligations.','original'),
('127.604.d.7.C',3,'The person who sells event space and services to clients and works with them to book dates is a sales:','["coordinator", "chef", "janitor", "driver"]'::jsonb,0,'Sales coordinators build client relationships.','original'),
('127.604.d.7.C',4,'A sales coordinator''s goals include booking events, answering client questions, and:','["hiding fees", "building repeat business", "avoiding follow-up", "discouraging inquiries"]'::jsonb,1,'Repeat clients are valuable.','original'),
('127.604.d.7.D',3,'If a client asks to cut catering costs, a planner may modify the menu by choosing less expensive:','["fonts", "flights", "dishes", "flowers"]'::jsonb,2,'Menu changes can fit the budget.','original'),
('127.604.d.7.D',4,'When evaluating catering options, a planner should compare price per person, quality, and ability to meet:','["parking limits", "birthday dates", "staff hobbies", "dietary needs"]'::jsonb,3,'Guests'' needs shape choices.','original'),
('127.604.d.7.E',3,'Rows of chairs facing a speaker with no tables is called a theater-style or:','["auditorium arrangement", "boardroom arrangement", "banquet arrangement", "cabaret arrangement"]'::jsonb,0,'Seating style depends on the event.','original'),
('127.604.d.7.E',4,'For a training session where attendees take notes, a planner would usually choose which arrangement?','["theater", "classroom", "open standing", "cocktail reception"]'::jsonb,1,'Tables allow writing and materials.','original'),
('127.604.d.7.F',3,'A planner estimating how many servers, tables, and sound systems an event requires is determining the needed staff and:','["taxes", "gifts", "resources", "rumors"]'::jsonb,2,'Planning matches needs to supply.','original'),
('127.604.d.7.F',4,'If the guest count doubles, the planner must increase staff and supplies in proportion to meet the specific:','["dates", "fears", "costs", "needs"]'::jsonb,3,'Plans scale with demand.','original'),
('127.604.d.8.A',3,'In an event company, a team leader reports to a department head, who reports to the owner. These are different levels of management:','["structure", "uniform", "decor", "menu"]'::jsonb,0,'Management has levels from top to bottom.','original'),
('127.604.d.8.A',4,'The chain of command shows who a worker reports to and who has the authority to:','["order lunch", "make decisions", "choose music only", "set the weather"]'::jsonb,1,'Structure clarifies authority.','original'),
('127.604.d.8.B',3,'A resort offers scenery and lodging, but it is far from an airport. This is a disadvantage of the destination because guests may find it:','["too close", "too cheap", "hard to reach", "too quiet to hear"]'::jsonb,2,'Access affects attendance.','original'),
('127.604.d.8.B',4,'Convenient parking, nearby hotels, and meeting rooms are advantages that make a facility:','["unusable", "less profitable", "too accessible", "attractive to planners"]'::jsonb,3,'Facilities are chosen for convenience.','original'),
('127.604.d.8.C',3,'A company that employs its own event planner for internal meetings has an in-house:','["event manager", "sponsor", "caterer", "vendor"]'::jsonb,0,'In-house planners work for the organization.','original'),
('127.604.d.8.C',4,'An in-house planner''s duties often include scheduling meetings, booking rooms, and managing the:','["landscaping", "budget", "sports teams", "parking tickets"]'::jsonb,1,'They support their own organization.','original'),
('127.604.d.8.D',3,'When working with an outside hotel for a conference, the planner''s main role is to coordinate with the hotel''s:','["guests only", "security vendors only", "sales and catering staff", "laundry staff only"]'::jsonb,2,'Planners and venues must communicate.','original'),
('127.604.d.8.D',4,'A planner and a venue manager confirm details in advance to avoid:','["receiving revenue", "saving time", "cutting costs", "double booking and misunderstandings"]'::jsonb,3,'Coordination prevents problems.','original'),
('127.604.d.9.A',3,'Venue rental, catering, and printing are examples of an event''s:','["expenses", "revenues", "profits", "grants"]'::jsonb,0,'Expenses are costs of planning and production.','original'),
('127.604.d.9.A',4,'Adding up all planned costs before the event helps a planner create the event''s:','["guest list", "budget", "floor plan", "schedule"]'::jsonb,1,'A budget compares costs with funds.','original'),
('127.604.d.9.B',3,'Offering an early-bird discount to boost ticket sales is a marketing technique that can improve:','["costs", "waste", "profitability", "delays"]'::jsonb,2,'Marketing brings in revenue.','original'),
('127.604.d.9.B',4,'A marketing technique like partnering with a local business to share promotions can reach new:','["regulators", "banks", "landlords", "audiences"]'::jsonb,3,'Partners expand reach.','original'),
('127.604.d.9.C',3,'A caterer charges $18 per person and 120 guests are expected. The cost of the meal is:','["$2,160", "$216", "$1,800", "$2,016"]'::jsonb,0,'18 times 120 equals 2,160.','original'),
('127.604.d.9.C',4,'Linens cost $4 each, and the event needs 45 tables with one linen per table. The total for linens is:','["$225", "$180", "$90", "$49"]'::jsonb,1,'4 times 45 equals 180.','original'),
('127.604.d.9.D',3,'Labor costs for hourly workers are called:','["marketing costs", "tax credits", "payroll expenses", "sales revenue"]'::jsonb,2,'Payroll affects profit.','original'),
('127.604.d.9.D',4,'Five workers each earn $15 an hour and work 6 hours. The payroll expense is:','["$90", "$30", "$75", "$450"]'::jsonb,3,'5 times 15 times 6 equals 450.','original'),
('127.604.d.9.E',3,'If an event runs over budget, the planner might modify operating procedures to cut waste, such as ordering supplies:','["in bulk", "from anyone", "last minute", "twice"]'::jsonb,0,'Procedures can be adjusted to control costs.','original'),
('127.604.d.9.E',4,'Changing the way staff set up tables so the job takes less time is a modification to operating:','["guests", "procedures", "vendors", "revenues"]'::jsonb,1,'Efficiency lowers cost.','original'),
('127.604.d.9.F',3,'A planner creating a marketing plan for weddings and government meetings must consider that each market has different:','["time zones only", "logos only", "needs and budgets", "birthdays only"]'::jsonb,2,'Different markets require different approaches.','original'),
('127.604.d.9.F',4,'Government clients often follow strict purchasing rules, so a marketing plan should highlight:','["flashy gifts", "lower quality", "secrecy", "compliance and transparency"]'::jsonb,3,'Government buyers value rules.','original'),
('127.604.d.9.G',3,'An event brings in $12,000 and costs $9,000. The profit is:','["$3,000", "$21,000", "$9,000", "$12,000"]'::jsonb,0,'12,000 minus 9,000 equals 3,000.','original'),
('127.604.d.9.G',4,'A profit margin of 25 percent on $20,000 in sales means the profit is:','["$500", "$5,000", "$4,000", "$25,000"]'::jsonb,1,'25 percent of 20,000 is 5,000.','original'),
('127.604.d.9.H',3,'Surveying guests after an event is a(n):','["pre-event evaluation", "contract review", "post-event evaluation", "tax filing"]'::jsonb,2,'Feedback shows what worked.','original'),
('127.604.d.9.H',4,'A pre-event evaluation checks readiness, such as confirming vendors, while a post-event evaluation reviews:','["next year''s menu", "parking prices", "staff birthdays", "what happened and results"]'::jsonb,3,'Both support improvement.','original'),
('127.604.d.10.A',3,'Liability insurance protects an event organizer from costs if a guest is injured. The amount the insurance will pay is a liability:','["limit", "fee", "menu", "tax"]'::jsonb,0,'Policies set coverage limits.','original'),
('127.604.d.10.A',4,'A venue may require a planner to carry at least $1 million in insurance. This shows why planners must understand coverage:','["rumors", "requirements", "trends", "tickets"]'::jsonb,1,'Venues set insurance minimums.','original'),
('127.604.d.10.B',3,'If a client supplies their own insurance policy for an event, the planner must verify that it covers the date, location, and:','["guest names", "music playlist", "type of event", "caterer''s fees"]'::jsonb,2,'Coverage must match the event.','original'),
('127.604.d.10.B',4,'Some venues allow clients to buy one-day event coverage, which protects against property damage and:','["traffic", "menu errors", "weather forecasts", "guest injuries"]'::jsonb,3,'One-day policies are common.','original'),
('127.604.d.10.C',3,'Planners must ensure fire exits are clear, food is safe, and capacity is not exceeded to meet legal, health, and safety:','["obligations", "habits", "trends", "rumors"]'::jsonb,0,'Safety is a legal duty.','original'),
('127.604.d.10.C',4,'Posting a venue''s maximum occupancy and not allowing more guests to enter helps meet safety:','["fashions", "regulations", "goals", "hobbies"]'::jsonb,1,'Capacity limits protect people.','original'),
('127.604.d.10.D',3,'Hosting an event where drinks are served can make the host legally responsible if a guest is hurt after drinking. This is a legal:','["advantage", "discount", "implication", "holiday"]'::jsonb,2,'Providing alcohol creates liability.','original'),
('127.604.d.10.D',4,'To reduce risk at an event that serves alcohol, a planner can hire trained servers, check IDs, and arrange safe:','["décor", "entertainment", "parking fees", "transportation"]'::jsonb,3,'Responsible service reduces harm.','original'),
('127.604.d.10.E',3,'Large public events often need coordination with police and fire officials for crowd control and emergency access. These are law enforcement:','["requirements", "rumors", "gifts", "trends"]'::jsonb,0,'Authorities set rules for public safety.','original'),
('127.604.d.10.E',4,'A planner of a street festival typically applies for a permit and meets city safety and traffic:','["trophies", "rules", "debts", "menus"]'::jsonb,1,'Permits ensure public safety.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
